{"id": "EUVD-2026-98706", "enisaUuid": "2e50f180-1e0b-3af5-97f5-7f490b8c07c5", "description": "FreeRDP from 2.3.0 before 3.32.0 contains an infinite loop vulnerability in http_chuncked_read that allows malicious RD Gateways to hang clients by sending incomplete chunked responses. Attackers can send a partial chunk-size line or footer followed by a clean TLS shutdown, causing zero-byte reads to loop forever and freeze the client decoder thread.", "datePublished": "2026-10-13T13:27:10", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-18T12:08:12", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/FreeRDP/FreeRDP/security/advisories/GHSA-7vfc-chg9-q5r8", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/freerdp-2.3.0-before-3.32.0-infinite-loop-via-rd-gateway-chunked-response"], "aliases": ["GHSA-26h4-ghv8-j876", "CVE-2026-109941"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.27, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "9369d7fa-d8be-39a3-9fb2-098be4df3af5", "product": {"name": "FreeRDP", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}, "product_version": "2.3.0 <3.32.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "0d2972d9-dfa6-3301-89e5-7482ccb31575", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}], "isExploited": false}